####################################################################
# cat2_lift.rq — CAT2 lift condition. HAND-AUTHORED.
#
# A CAT2 silence (CAT2a or CAT2b) holds only while an active alarm
# justifies it (agreed 2026-09-21): every active alarm that justified it at
# arrival, under either rule, is stored as `incoming mdapoc:silencedBy
# active` in the incoming alarm's own transient graph (so it disappears
# when that alarm ends). When an active alarm ends, its silencedBy links
# are removed (actions/silence_lift_delete.rq); an alarm left with none
# from either rule, and still active, has its silence lifted — logged as a
# cat2_lifted firing. One silence per alarm, whatever the rules behind it:
# that is how it is presented to a clinician.
#
# This condition finds the alarms whose silence is lifted: silenced by the
# ended alarm, still active after it, and silenced by nothing else.
#
# CONTRACT. Bound on entry: ?ended (the alarm that just ended), ?now.
# Binds: ?silenced. Used by actions/silence_lift_select.rq.
#
# VALIDATION — engine/regression.py: cat2a_lift, cat2b_lift and cat3f are
# lifted; cat2a_lift_last only when the LAST justifying alarm ends
# (forbidden firing at the first one's end).
####################################################################

PREFIX mdapoc: <https://w3id.org/mda/poc#>

GRAPH ?gS { ?silenced mdapoc:silencedBy ?ended }
# the silenced alarm is still active strictly after ?now
?gS mdapoc:validUntil ?gS_until . FILTER(?now < ?gS_until)
FILTER NOT EXISTS { GRAPH ?gS2 { ?silenced mdapoc:silencedBy ?other } FILTER(?other != ?ended) }
